# Example only — no values here, and this is the only environment file that is
# committed. The code reads the process environment, not this file: nothing in
# the project loads a .env, on purpose. Making the live path easy to trigger
# would work against the design, which is that the suite cannot call a paid API
# by accident. Export these two deliberately, in the shell, when you mean to
# record:
#
#   export ECLUSA_LIVE=1
#   export OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
#   make record
#
# Without ECLUSA_LIVE=1 the provider replays recordings and never calls out.
# With ECLUSA_LIVE=1 and no key it refuses rather than guessing.

ECLUSA_LIVE=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
